{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Please let my lord pass on.</b> Do not lengthen the days of your journey — go according to your pace, even if you go far ahead." "<b>I will lead on.</b> אֶתְנַהֵל — the heh is superfluous, like אֵרְדָה, אֶשְׁמְעָה." "<b>Gently.</b> לְאַט שֶׁלִּי — a term of leisurely pace, those who walk slowly: ״לְאַט לִי לַנַּעַר״ (II Samuel 18). The lamed of לְאִטִּי is from the root, and it serves — אֶתְנַהֵל: a leisurely pace." "<b>At the pace of the work.</b> According to the need of the foot-journey of the work imposed upon me to conduct." "<b>And at the pace of the children.</b> According to their feet — what they are able to walk." "<b>Until I come to my lord at Seir.</b> He lengthened the road for him, for his intention was to go only as far as Succot. He said: If his intention is to do me harm, let him wait until I come to him — and he never went. And when will he go? In the days of the Messiah (Bereshit Rabbah), as it is said: ״וְעָלוּ מוֹשִׁעִים בְּהַר צִיּוֹן לִשְׁפֹּט אֶת הַר עֵשָׂו״ (Obadiah 1); and from this verse there are many interpretations."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:59.941285807Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}